# U007 mkdir option snapshot amendment

The original U007 feature, README, capture index, raw streams and source snapshots
remain historical, unchanged evidence. This additive contract covers the
subsequently demonstrated changing-options defect.

Before deciding whether mkdir can establish exclusive provenance, capture its
closed `recursive` and `mode` values once. Both the invocation observer and the
filesystem call use those captured values, not the original accessors. The
adapter receives a frozen data snapshot; retaining the caller options object's
identity is deliberately not part of the adapter contract.

An existing root that yields the original `EEXIST` grants no ownership. Cleanup
must neither adopt that root nor delete its sentinel. Recursive creation still
passes to the original mkdir and grants no exclusive provenance. Calls outside
the current active invocation continue to receive their original arguments.

`tests\u007-mkdir-snapshot.test.cjs` exercises direct and observed mkdir against
native-compatible, deterministic mkdir semantics. Its two original assertions
failed against the retained, loadable production baseline before the repair.
The same test bytes are replayed unchanged against the repaired implementation.
No actual neighbour is destroyed by the RED fixture.

This amendment does not qualify a browser, alter accepted U004-U006 production
or imports, rewrite old evidence, authorize live application, or award credit.
Current production coverage, mutation and namespace gates must be recaptured
for the repaired source rather than borrowed from the original source.
